  m_text: 'This is probably what most people think of when they consider arcade games.
    Video games in the arcade can differ widely by genres of games, but most of them
    share the same philosophy established by Atari co-founder Nolan Bushnell: they
    should be easy to learn, but hard to master. Ever since 1971, arcade video games
    have become a defining feature of all arcades and helped lay the foundation for
    the video game industry we know today. '
