  m_text: Pinball is another classic arcade game, estimated to have come onto the
    scene around 1931. In this game, the player launches a small metal ball into
    a table, where the ball can bounce between several different obstacles. The player
    uses flippers near the bottom to keep the ball from dropping to the bottom, while
    racking up as many points as they can.
